  "behavior": [
    "InvalidLexerStateLimit rejects fewer than two sentinel states before grammar compilation and at independently callable leaf entries.",
    "Finite cap installed before sentinel construction. All-lexeme selection, first-byte warming, large-lexeme precompute, initial row and initial skip preserve typed failure before publishing malformed parser state.",
    "Exact observed constructor count N succeeds and N-1 rejects. Precompute tests prove actual selected weight exceeds 1000 and distinguish original fuel failure.",
    "Deep clones preserve per-instance state cap and independent state/error; nonzero token streams prove runtime exhaustion and mask/commit parity.",
    "Matcher preserves only known closed configuration/ParserError causes and stop classification through repeated returns and copies. Original unrelated error payload retires before publication.",
    "After caught recognizer panic, optional cause inspection uses try_lock and does not recover poisoned state, block, or panic again. Original terminal failure is preserved."
  ],
  "initial_failures": [],
  "limits": [
    "State count is not a full parser byte bound: expression and derivative/relevance caches, candidate vectors, parser rows/history/captures, compiler/tokenizer/slicer owners and copy peaks remain separate.",
